UPDATE companies SET description='Accu-Mold Plastics was founded in 1972 by Jack L. Strohecker and his wife Mary Lou in the basement of their Halifax, Pennsylvania home. Originally named Accu-Mold & Tool Company, the business began as a precision mold and die operation serving the electronics industry. Early clients such as American Catheter Company and Hamilton Watch helped the shop expand beyond tooling into injection molding, and by 1973 the company had installed its first automatic molding machine.

Today the company operates a 9,000-square-foot facility equipped with automated injection molding presses ranging from 22 to 125 tons of clamping force and shot capacities of 1.2 to nearly 9 ounces. Its in-house tool room provides CNC machining, sinker EDM, surface grinding, manual machining, and heat treating, supporting complete mold design, construction, and repair. A geothermal-controlled clean room enables contamination-free molding for medical and electronic components, while overmolding and insert molding capabilities allow multi-material assemblies. The shop handles everything from single-cavity prototypes to full-scale production runs, with value-added services including assembly, packaging, and just-in-time delivery.

Accu-Mold serves the electronics and medical device sectors, with a historic focus on medical disposables and start-up companies needing high-quality molds to compete against larger rivals. Current customers include firms in electronics and medical disposables, though specific names are not disclosed.

The company emphasizes efficiency, competitive pricing, and customer support, leveraging modern molding technologies and streamlined processes to keep clients competitive. Its founding vision was to deliver high-quality precision molds and components to the electronics industry, a mission that has expanded to include comprehensive in-house design, tooling, and molding under one roof.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision injection molding", "Mold design and engineering", "In-house mold building and tooling", "CNC machining", "Sinker EDM", "Surface grinding", "Manual machining", "Heat treating", "Overmolding", "Insert molding", "Clean room molding", "Prototyping (single cavity)", "Full-scale production", "Part assembly", "Packaging", "Just-in-time delivery", "Quality inspection and control", "Mold maintenance and repair", "Tooling design and development"], "industries": ["Electronics", "Medical devices", "Medical disposables"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (22-125 ton)", "CNC machining centers", "Sinker EDM machines", "Surface grinders", "Heat treating furnaces", "Geothermal-controlled clean room"], "volume": "Prototype to full-scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Complete in-house mold design, tooling, and injection molding", "Geothermal-controlled clean room for contamination-free production", "Overmolding and insert molding capabilities", "Prototype to high-volume production flexibility", "In-house CNC machining, EDM, and heat treating for tooling"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 by Jack L. Strohecker and Mary Lou Strohecker in Halifax, PA -> /about", "Started as Accu-Mold & Tool Company in basement -> /about", "Early clients: American Catheter Company, Hamilton Watch -> /about", "First automatic injection molding machine acquired 1973 -> /about", "9,000 sq ft facility built 1985 with CNC and EDM -> /about", "Tornado 2006 destroyed facility, rebuilt in 8 days with clean r