UPDATE companies SET description='Luvata Waterbury operates from a facility on Thomaston Avenue in Waterbury, Connecticut. The business traces its roots to 1971 with the founding of Intermagnetics General Corporation (IGC). Outokumpu Copper Products Oy acquired IGC Advanced Superconductors in 2001 and rebranded the operation as Luvata in 2006. Mitsubishi Materials Corporation purchased Luvata in May 2017, making the Waterbury site a subsidiary of the Japanese materials group.

The plant specializes in manufacturing copper-stabilized niobium-titanium (NbTi) and niobium-tin (Nb3Sn) conductors for low-temperature superconducting applications. Its product line covers superconducting wire and cable used in magnetic resonance imaging systems, particle accelerators, and fusion energy research. The site employs a team of over 100 professionals focused on innovation and production excellence.

Customers span medical diagnostic imaging, high-energy physics, and nuclear fusion sectors. Luvata Waterbury superconductors have been specified for the Large Hadron Collider at CERN, the KSTAR fusion research project in Korea, the International Thermonuclear Experimental Reactor (ITER), and a $6.5 million supply contract for CEA Saclay in France. A $26 million U.S. Department of Energy fusion contract was awarded in 2009.

The company positions itself as a recognized leader in superconductive wire supply where delivery and performance are critical. Its selection for flagship international science projects and long-standing ISO 9001 and ISO 14001:2015 certifications underscore a focus on quality and environmental management.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Superconducting wire manufacturing", "Superconducting cable manufacturing", "Copper-stabilized NbTi conductor production", "Copper-stabilized Nb3Sn conductor production", "Low-temperature superconducting (LTS) wire production"], "industries": ["Medical diagnostic systems (MRI)", "High energy physics", "Nuclear fusion research", "Particle accelerator components"], "materials": ["Copper", "NbTi (Niobium-Titanium)", "Nb3Sn (Niobium-Tin)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Selected for LHC at CERN, KSTAR, and ITER projects", "Over 100 professionals dedicated to superconducting wire innovation", "ISO 9001 and ISO 14001:2015 certified", "Copper-stabilized NbTi and Nb3Sn conductor expertise"], "facts_used": ["Location: Waterbury, CT -> /", "Founded 1971 as IGC -> /", "Outokumpu acquisition 2001 -> /", "Rebranded Luvata 2006 -> /", "Mitsubishi Materials acquisition 2017 -> /about-us", "Over 100 employees -> /", "ISO 9001 and ISO 14001:2015 -> /", "Products: NbTi and Nb3Sn superconducting wire/cable -> /", "Industries: MRI, high energy physics, fusion -> /", "Projects: LHC, KSTAR, ITER, CEA Saclay -> /", "DOE $26M contract 2009 -> /", "Address: 2121 Thomaston Avenue, Waterbury, CT 06704 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Luvata in Waterbury, Connecticut specializes in manufacturing copper stabilized NbTi and Nb3Sn conductors", "founded_year": "1971", "employee_count": "100+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}':