UPDATE companies SET description='Advanced Food Technologies, operating as Roskam Foods, is headquartered in Grand Rapids, Michigan. Founded in 1923 as a single-product operation, the company has grown into one of the largest multi-category external food manufacturers in the United States. The business is investor-backed and employs approximately 2,400 people across eight facilities in the U.S. and Canada.

The company provides co-manufacturing services for branded food companies, national retailers, and private-label partners. Its processing platforms include twin- and single-screw extrusion for direct-expanded cereals, protein crisps, and snack puffs; end-to-end baking with dough mixing, sheeting, proofing, baking, and tempering; specialty snack processing such as drying, seasoning, air popping, and particulate application; and advanced packaging in stand-up pouches, dual-compartment cups, bag-in-box, and bulk super-sacks. In-house engineering supports feasibility studies, line design, capital assessments, and turnkey capital project management. The combined footprint exceeds two million square feet of manufacturing and warehouse space with more than 50 production and packaging lines.

Roskam serves the snack food, confectionery, frozen meal, pizza dough, dry baking mix, cereal, and granola categories. Its five specialized platforms—Baked Snacks & Popcorns, Frozen Foods, Dry Mix Blending, Cereal & Granola, and Confectionary—span frozen, refrigerated, and shelf-stable temperature states. Customers include national brands, store-brand programs, and private-label partners seeking large-scale, multi-category production consolidation.

The company emphasizes a partner-first mindset, disciplined execution, and continuous investment in new technologies and formats. All facilities hold SQF Level II and III certification, with additional USDA Organic, Non-GMO Project Verified, Keto Certified, Fair Trade, and Kosher certifications. Dedicated peanut-free facilities and controlled allergen protocols address sensitive ingredient handling. Integrated R&D, packaging development, supply chain logistics, and project management support take concepts from ideation through commercialization.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF Level II','SQF Level III','USDA Organic','Non-GMO Project Verified','Keto Certified','Fair Trade','Kosher']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Twin-screw extrusion", "Single-screw extrusion", "Direct-expanded cereal production", "Protein crisp manufacturing", "Snack puff production", "Dough mixing", "Sheeting", "Proofing", "Baking", "Tempering", "Drying", "Seasoning (slurry/topical oil)", "Air popping", "Topical particulate application", "Stand-up resealable pouch packaging", "Dual-compartment cup packaging", "Bag-in-box packaging", "Bulk super-sack packaging", "Feasibility studies", "Line design", "Capital assessments", "New-product commercialization", "Turnkey capital project management", "Custom line design"], "industries": ["Snack Foods", "Confections & Candy", "Frozen Meals", "Pizza Dough", "Dry Baking Mixes", "Cereal and Granola", "Baked Snacks & Popcorns", "Frozen Foods", "Dry Mix Blending", "Confectionary", "Better-for-You / Organic / Non-GMO / Gluten-Free / Grain-Free"], "materials": ["Organic ingredients", "Non-GMO ingredients", "Gluten-free ingredients", "Grain-free ingredients", "Peanuts", "Tree nuts"], "equipment": ["Twin-screw extrusion lines", "Single-screw extrusion lines", "Pilot lines for scalability testing"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All facilities SQF Level II & III certified with multiple dietary certifications", "Dedicated peanut-free 